        <headline>Wind Advisory issued September 23 at 10:54AM AKDT until September 24 at 10:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Southeast winds 35 to 45 mph with gusts up to 55 mph
expected.

* WHERE...Northern Bristol Bay Coast.

* WHEN...From 7 AM to 10 PM AKDT Thursday.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects and a few
power outages may result.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A strong front moving inland from the eastern
Bering will bring gusty southeasterly winds to the Southwest
coastline beginning Thursday morning. Winds are expected to peak
around noon through 4pm AKDT Thursday, then steadily diminish
through Thursday evening.
</description>
        <instruction>Winds this strong can make driving difficult.</instruction>
